\subsection{Sentiment Analysis}
\label{subsection:sentiment}
Sentiment Analysis is the process of determining the polarity, subjectivity, or emotion of a sentence or phrase. Some common applications of Sentiment Analysis include analyzing product reviews, news, and financial documents. To create a dataset for this task, we scraped a website that hosts movie reviews from users of the popular social media platform Reddit. The dataset was labeled with the score assigned to the review, from 1 (very negative) to 5 (very positive).

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Instruction:} Rephrase the following text so that it's easier to read. Please write a short paragraph that says the same thing, but in a more understandable way.
    \item \textbf{Input:} Her father Francis Van Arnum Brown worked at a number of jobs including as a clerk at the Washington Patent Office and as a manager and salesman for a wholesale butcher.

\begin{solution}
In our experiments we've found that the RNNs often do not learn the necessary representations to produce good results. This can be attributed to the difficulty of the problem itself, but also the complexity of the training task. To simplify this task we restrict the vocabulary and provide a simplified input (as described above). We then provide the following as a ground truth:

"Laura Bacall, born September, is an American film and stage actress and model, known for her distinctive husky voice and sultry looks."
\end{solution}
